body.statement:
Suppose treatment adoption is staggered over time. Under Chen, Sant'Anna, and Xie's Assumptions S, O, NA, and PT-All, if \(\operatorname{IF}^{\operatorname{att}(g,t)}_{\mathrm{stg}}\) is their stacked influence-function vector and \(\Omega_{gt}(X)\) is its conditional covariance matrix, then the efficient influence function of \(\operatorname{ATT}(g,t)\) is
\[
\operatorname{EIF}^{\operatorname{att}(g,t)}_{\mathrm{stg}}
=\frac{\mathbf 1'\Omega_{gt}(X)^{-1}}{\mathbf 1'\Omega_{gt}(X)^{-1}\mathbf 1}
\operatorname{IF}^{\operatorname{att}(g,t)}_{\mathrm{stg}}.
\]
